  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Given name then family name, often with a middle name. The most common surnames are -son patronymics frozen in the 1800s (Andersson, Johansson); others are 'nature' names made up then (Lindberg, Lundgren). Everyone is on first-name terms with 'du', including bosses. Finnish is an official minority language and Sweden Finns keep Finnish names. Swedes with Arab, Kurdish, Persian, Somali, Polish or Balkan roots usually keep family names from their parents' language; Polish women's surnames end in -ska, and Bosnian, Croatian and Serbian surnames often end in -ić.",
